<title>SOUTH KOREA: South Korea's Q1 oil products demand edge lower.</title>
<headline>South Korea's Q1 oil products demand edge lower.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's petroleum products demand fell 0.4 percent to 204.0 million barrels in the first quarter of 1997 from 204.8 million barrels a year ago, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Monday.</p>
<p>In comparison, consumption rose 9.6 percent in the first quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>A ministry statement cited slower industrial growth, an active energy conservation campaign and higher demand for liquefied natural gas, as the prime reasons for the negative growth.  </p>
<p>Oil products demand (in million barrels)</p>
<p>				    Q1/1997	  Q1/1996</p>
<p>    TOTAL			  204.0	    204.8</p>
<p>MAJOR PRODUCTS</p>
<p>     gasoline		     15.8	     15.8</p>
<p>     kerosene		     30.7	     29.7</p>
<p>     diesel			 45.3	     50.9</p>
<p>     C-type fuel oil	    45.9	     44.5</p>
<p>     naphtha			38.7	     36.4</p>
<p>     LPG			    20.3	     20.5</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
